# bblayers.conf.sample — Copy this to your build/conf/bblayers.conf
# and adjust the absolute paths to match your workspace layout.
#
# bblayers.conf tells BitBake which layers to include in the build.
# BBLAYERS is an ordered list of absolute paths to layer root directories
# (the directory containing conf/layer.conf).
#
# Layer order matters for BBFILE_PRIORITY tie-breaking, but explicit
# priority values in layer.conf are the primary mechanism.

# BBPATH and BBFILES are set automatically by BitBake using the layer
# information — you don't set them here.

BBLAYERS ?= " \
  /path/to/workspace/poky/meta \
  /path/to/workspace/poky/meta-poky \
  /path/to/workspace/poky/meta-yocto-bsp \
  /path/to/workspace/meta-beaglebone-bsp \
  "

# NOTES:
#
# poky/meta          = OE-Core: the base recipes (busybox, glibc, kernel, etc.)
# poky/meta-poky     = Poky distro layer: sets poky distro defaults
# poky/meta-yocto-bsp = Yocto reference BSPs (qemu targets, etc.)
# meta-beaglebone-bsp = Our custom BSP layer for the BeagleBone Black
#
# When using the new bitbake-setup init workflow (Whinlatter 5.3+), the
# paths to the poky layers will be inside the setup directory created by
# bitbake-setup. Check the auto-generated bblayers.conf for the correct
# paths, then add meta-beaglebone-bsp to the end of BBLAYERS.
